{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016jMa9M52MnwjYS4M4Qo9Vr","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Pareto Dominance Analysis — Verification Report\n2\t\n3\t**Date**: 2026-05-21\n4\t**Script**: `code/pareto_analysis.py`\n5\t**Data**: Qwen2.5-7B MVP (westd-13176), zero_shot method\n6\t\n7\t## Verification Summary\n8\t\n9\tScript ran successfully on MVP data. All 3 output files produced: `pareto_detail.csv`, `pareto_summary.csv`, `pareto_results.json`.\n10\t\n11\t## Results (Qwen2.5-7B, 8 layers x 5 languages)\n12\t\n13\t| Language | Pareto Layers | HV | Spearman rho | p-value | Tradeoff? |\n14\t|----------|---------------|------|------------|---------|-----------|\n15\t| zh | [24, 27] | 0.0456 | +0.857 | 0.0065 | Local only |\n16\t| ar | [24, 27] | 0.0370 | +0.857 | 0.0065 | Local only |\n17\t| hi | [20, 27] | 0.0369 | +0.310 | 0.4556 | Local only |\n18\t| ko | [24, 27] | 0.0360 | +0.714 | 0.0465 | Local only |\n19\t| sw | [27] | 0.0148 | +0.762 | 0.0280 | None |\n20\t\n21\t## Key Findings\n22\t\n23\t### L27 is universally Pareto-optimal\n24\tL27 (EN AUROC = 0.746, best) appears on every language's Pareto front, confirming it as the best EN probe layer.\n25\t\n26\t### Tradeoff is local, not global\n27\tSpearman rho is **positive** for all languages (EN and ZS AUROC generally co-increase with depth). The tradeoff manifests only at the top of the frontier:\n28\t\n29\t- **zh**: L24 (ZS=0.686) > L27 (ZS=0.661), but L27 EN > L24 EN -- both Pareto-optimal\n30\t- **ar**: L24 (ZS=0.651) > L27 (ZS=0.635), same pattern\n31\t- **hi**: L20 (ZS=0.652) > L27 (ZS=0.626), deeper tradeoff -- middle layer wins transfer\n32\t- **ko**: L24 (ZS=0.648) > L27 (ZS=0.607), similar to zh/ar\n33\t- **sw**: L27 dominates all layers on both objectives -- no tradeoff\n34\t\n35\t### Interpretation for C4 response\n36\tThe Pareto analysis reveals a **nuanced** tradeoff:\n37\t1. The global correlation is positive -- deeper layers are generally better for both EN and transfer.\n38\t2. But the **frontier** shows a local tradeoff at L24-L27: the best EN layer (L27) is NOT the best transfer layer for 4/5 languages.\n39\t3. Hypervolume is largest for zh (0.046) and smallest for sw (0.015), suggesting the tradeoff is language-dependent and correlates with typological distance.\n40\t\n41\t### Validation checks\n42\t- L27 on Pareto front for all languages (expected: best EN)\n43\t- L24 or L20 as second Pareto point where tradeoff exists (expected: best transfer)\n44\t- sw has no tradeoff -- L27 dominates (consistent with sw being lowest-resource, weakest transfer overall)\n45\t- Hypervolume ordering (zh > ar > hi > ko > sw) roughly tracks overall transfer quality\n46\t\n47\t## Output Files\n48\t- `results/pareto/pareto_detail.csv` -- 40 rows (8 layers x 5 langs), with is_pareto_optimal and pareto_rank\n49\t- `results/pareto/pareto_summary.csv` -- 5 rows, per-language hypervolume + Spearman\n50\t- `results/pareto/pareto_results.json` -- combined structured output\n51\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9de67d78-cf2b-4095-b998-834caafee25d","uuid":"ab7b2626-a547-43b0-9331-8a434ee3adb4","timestamp":"2026-05-21T05:07:24.255Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0519_2/projects/xling_calib_direction/artifacts/pareto_analysis_verified.md","content":"# Pareto Dominance Analysis — Verification Report\n\n**Date**: 2026-05-21\n**Script**: `code/pareto_analysis.py`\n**Data**: Qwen2.5-7B MVP (westd-13176), zero_shot method\n\n## Verification Summary\n\nScript ran successfully on MVP data. All 3 output files produced: `pareto_detail.csv`, `pareto_summary.csv`, `pareto_results.json`.\n\n## Results (Qwen2.5-7B, 8 layers x 5 languages)\n\n| Language | Pareto Layers | HV | Spearman rho | p-value | Tradeoff? |\n|----------|---------------|------|------------|---------|-----------|\n| zh | [24, 27] | 0.0456 | +0.857 | 0.0065 | Local only |\n| ar | [24, 27] | 0.0370 | +0.857 | 0.0065 | Local only |\n| hi | [20, 27] | 0.0369 | +0.310 | 0.4556 | Local only |\n| ko | [24, 27] | 0.0360 | +0.714 | 0.0465 | Local only |\n| sw | [27] | 0.0148 | +0.762 | 0.0280 | None |\n\n## Key Findings\n\n### L27 is universally Pareto-optimal\nL27 (EN AUROC = 0.746, best) appears on every language's Pareto front, confirming it as the best EN probe layer.\n\n### Tradeoff is local, not global\nSpearman rho is **positive** for all languages (EN and ZS AUROC generally co-increase with depth). The tradeoff manifests only at the top of the frontier:\n\n- **zh**: L24 (ZS=0.686) > L27 (ZS=0.661), but L27 EN > L24 EN -- both Pareto-optimal\n- **ar**: L24 (ZS=0.651) > L27 (ZS=0.635), same pattern\n- **hi**: L20 (ZS=0.652) > L27 (ZS=0.626), deeper tradeoff -- middle layer wins transfer\n- **ko**: L24 (ZS=0.648) > L27 (ZS=0.607), similar to zh/ar\n- **sw**: L27 dominates all layers on both objectives -- no tradeoff\n\n### Interpretation for C4 response\nThe Pareto analysis reveals a **nuanced** tradeoff:\n1. The global correlation is positive -- deeper layers are generally better for both EN and transfer.\n2. But the **frontier** shows a local tradeoff at L24-L27: the best EN layer (L27) is NOT the best transfer layer for 4/5 languages.\n3. Hypervolume is largest for zh (0.046) and smallest for sw (0.015), suggesting the tradeoff is language-dependent and correlates with typological distance.\n\n### Validation checks\n- L27 on Pareto front for all languages (expected: best EN)\n- L24 or L20 as second Pareto point where tradeoff exists (expected: best transfer)\n- sw has no tradeoff -- L27 dominates (consistent with sw being lowest-resource, weakest transfer overall)\n- Hypervolume ordering (zh > ar > hi > ko > sw) roughly tracks overall transfer quality\n\n## Output Files\n- `results/pareto/pareto_detail.csv` -- 40 rows (8 layers x 5 langs), with is_pareto_optimal and pareto_rank\n- `results/pareto/pareto_summary.csv` -- 5 rows, per-language hypervolume + Spearman\n- `results/pareto/pareto_results.json` -- combined structured output\n","numLines":51,"startLine":1,"totalLines":51}}}
